  message: "Satisfied. Merged 9db39694bc (selfh/dev, fast-forward). Behavioral repro on the MERGED code (re-ran the filed 'repo with examples/' repro): classify_file now returns tier 1 for examples/app.py (is_example=True), demos/widget.ts (is_example=True), docs/Documentation.docc/*.swift (reason 'documentation path matches'), analysis.ipynb (reason 'notebook file (.ipynb)'), fuzz/fuzz_targets/*.rs + benches/*.rs (reason 'fuzz/bench path matches') — all were tier 2 (INTERNAL_DEP) pre-fix. Genuine tier-2 preserved: libs/shared/u.py under config internal_package_roots -> tier 2 (now the SOLE tier-2 producer; no path heuristic yields tier 2). Generated in-repo routes promote tier 4->1 (was 2), asserted by the end-to-end run_behavior_map route-promotion test (test_max_tier.py). Production-path evidence: ~27 flipped fixture tests in test_supply_chain.py (TestInternalDepDetection examples, TestDocCClassification, TestNotebookClassification, TestFuzzBenchClassification, TestIsExampleFileAxis) exercise classify_file directly; TestRoleFlagMutualExclusion rescoped tier-independent. Spec §14 scope-note (which flagged this as the open follow-up) resolved. Latent on self-corpus (0 role-file tier-2 nodes) so no self-analysis count moves — not a quantitative bakeoff claim (no awaits_bakeoff_validation tag)."  # 1e3e
